1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
[Captioning sponsored
by A&E TELEVISION NETWORKS]

2
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
IT'S A FAIR PROSPECT.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
PRETTY ENOUGH,
I GRANT YOU.

4
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
OH, IT'S NOTHING TO PEMBERLY,
I KNOW.

5
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
BUT I MUST
SETTLE SOMEWHERE.

6
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
HAVE I YOUR APPROVAL?

7
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
YOU'LL FIND THE SOCIETY
SOMETHING SAVAGE.

8
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,000
COUNTRY MANNERS?

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,000
I THINK THEY'RE CHARMING.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
THEN YOU'D BETTER TAKE IT.

11
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,000
THANK YOU.

12
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,000
I SHALL.

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
I SHALL CLOSE
WITH THE ATTORNEY DIRECTLY.

14
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
( birds singing )

15
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Young woman in house:
LYDIA, THAT'S MINE!

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
IT'S MINE NOW.

17
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
YOU'D NEVER
WEAR IT, ANYWAY.

18
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
I WOULD, I WANTED
TO WEAR IT TODAY!

19
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
LOOK WHAT
YOU'VE DONE TO IT!

20
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
MAMMA! MAMMA! LYDIA
HAS TORN UP MY BONNET

21
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
MADE IT UP NEW,
AND SAYS

22
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,000
SHE WILL WEAR IT
TO CHURCH!

23
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,000
TELL HER SHE SHALL NOT!

24
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
I SHALL WEAR IT,
MAMMA!

25
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
IT'S ALL MY OWN WORK.

26
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
SHE WOULD BE
A FRIGHT IN IT

27
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
BECAUSE SHE IS TOO PLAIN
TO LOOK WELL IN IT!

28
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
NO. YOU SHALL
NOT HAVE IT!

29
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
MAMMA, TELL HER SO!

30
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
GIRLS! WOULD YOU TEAR
MY NERVES INTO SHREDS?

31
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
OH, LET HER HAVE IT,
KITTY, AND BE DONE.

32
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,000
BUT IT IS MINE!

33
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
YOU LET HER HAVE
EVERYTHING THAT IS MINE.

34
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,000
OH!

35
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
( slams door )

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
( sobs )

37
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Mamma:
OH, WHAT IS TO
BECOME OF US ALL?

38
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
JANE? LIZZY?

39
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
WHERE ARE YOU?

40
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
HERE, MAMMA.

41
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,000
COMING, MAMMA.

42
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:21,000
( general conversation )

43
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,000
MY DEAR!

44
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
MR. BENNET!

45
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
WONDERFUL NEWS!

46
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
NETHERFIELD PARK
IS LET AT LAST!

47
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
IS IT?

48
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
YES, IT IS, FOR
I HAVE JUST HAD IT

49
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
FROM MRS. LONG.

50
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
AND DO YOU NOT
WANT TO KNOW

51
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
WHO HAS TAKEN IT?

52
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
YOU WANT TO TELL ME

53
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
AND I HAVE NO OBJECTION
TO HEARING IT.

54
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,000
WHY, THEN, IT IS TAKEN

55
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
BY A YOUNG MAN
OF LARGE FORTUNE

56
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
FROM THE NORTH
OF ENGLAND.

57
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
A SINGLE MAN
OF LARGE FORTUNE, MY DEAR!

58
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
HE CAME DOWN
ON MONDAY

59
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
IN A CHAISE AND FOUR
TO SEE THE PLACE!

60
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
HIS NAME IS BINGLEY

61
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
AND HE WILL BE IN
POSSESSION BY MICHAELMAS!

62
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
AND HE HAS 5,000 A YEAR!

63
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
WHAT A FINE THING
FOR OUR GIRLS.

64
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
HOW SO? HOW CAN
IT AFFECT THEM?

65
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
OH, MR. BENNET

66
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,000
HOW CAN YOU BE
SO TIRESOME?!

67
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
OF COURSE, I
AM THINKING OF

68
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
HIS MARRYING
ONE OF THEM!

69
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
A SINGLE MAN
IN POSSESSION

70
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
OF A GOOD FORTUNE

71
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
MUST BE IN
WANT OF A WIFE.

72
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
YES, HE MUST, INDEED!

73
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
AND WHO BETTER THAN ONE
OF OUR FIVE GIRLS?

74
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
( Lydia giggles and snorts )

75
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
LYDIA!

76
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
WHAT A FINE JOKE
IF HE WERE TO CHOOSE ME!

77
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
OR ME!

78
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
SO, THAT IS HIS DESIGN
IN SETTLING HERE?

79
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
TO MARRY ONE
OF OUR DAUGHTERS?

80
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
DESIGN? OH, HOW CAN YOU
TALK SUCH NONSENSE?

81
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
BUT YOU KNOW,
HE MAY VERY LIKELY

82
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
FALL IN LOVE
WITH ONE OF THEM.

83
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
THEREFORE, YOU MUST VISIT
HIM DIRECTLY HE COMES.

84
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
VISIT HIM?
OH, NO, NO.

85
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
I SEE NO OCCASION
FOR THAT.

86
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
OH, MR. BENNET!

87
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
GO YOURSELF
WITH THE GIRLS.

88
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
OR STILL BETTER,
SEND THEM BY THEMSELVES.

89
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
BY THEMSELVES?!

90
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
AYE, FOR YOU'RE
AS HANDSOME

91
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
AS ANY OF THEM.

92
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
MR. BINGLEY MIGHT
LIKE YOU BEST.

93
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
LYDIA.
( giggling )

94
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Mrs. Bennet:
EVERYTHING I TRY TO DO
FOR YOU GIRLS

95
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
IS RUINED. RUINED!

96
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
NOBODY THINKS ABOUT
YOUR FUTURE BUT ME.

97
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
OH, HILL!

98
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
OH, HILL!

99
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,000
HILL, I AM
SO DISTRESSED...

100
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
FOR MR. BENNET SAYS

101
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
HE WILL NOT VISIT
MR. BINGLEY

102
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
WHEN HE COMES!

103
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
OH, THERE, THERE
NOW, MA'AM.

104
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
MAMMA, CAN'T YOU
REASON WITH HIM?

105
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
WHAT SHALL WE DO

106
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
IF WE'RE NOT ALLOWED
TO MEET ANYONE?

107
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
NO, NO,
IT WILL NOT BE WELL

108
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
FOR HE IS BENT ON
RUINING US ALL!

109
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
MAMMA, I'M SURE
HE IS TEASING YOU.

110
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
HE WILL CALL ON
MR. BINGLEY

111
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
AS HE WOULD
ANY NEW NEIGHBOR.

112
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,000
NO, NO, JANE,
HOW CAN YOU SAY THAT?

113
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,000
YOU HEARD HIM YOURSELF

114
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
AND YOU KNOW THAT
YOUR FATHER HAS A WILL OF IRON.

115
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
YOU'RE IN THE RIGHT,
MY DEAR.

116
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
BUT I'LL TELL YOU
WHAT I'LL DO.

117
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
I SHALL WRITE
TO MR. BINGLEY

118
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
INFORMING HIM
THAT I HAVE FIVE DAUGHTERS

119
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
AND HE IS WELCOME TO
ANY OF THEM THAT HE CHOOSES!

120
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
THEY'RE SILLY AND IGNORANT,
LIKE OTHER GIRLS.

121
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
WELL, LIZZY HAS A LITTLE
MORE WIT THAN THE REST...

122
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
BUT HE MAY PREFER
A STUPID WIFE

123
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,000
AS OTHERS HAVE DONE BEFORE HIM.

124
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
THERE, WILL THAT DO?

125
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
NO, NO! I BEG YOU WILL NOT
WRITE AT ALL IF YOU...

126
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
OH, YOU TAKE DELIGHT
IN VEXING ME.

127
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
YOU HAVE NO COMPASSION
ON MY POOR NERVES.

128
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
YOU MISTAKE ME, MY DEAR.

129
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
I HAVE A HIGH RESPECT
FOR YOUR NERVES.

130
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
THEY'VE BEEN MY OLD FRIENDS
THESE 20 YEARS.

131
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
YOU DON'T KNOW WHAT I SUFFER!

132
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
WELL, I HOPE
YOU WILL GET OVER IT

133
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,000
AND LIVE TO SEE

134
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
MANY YOUNG MEN
OF 5,000 A YEAR

135
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
COME INTO
THE NEIGHBORHOOD.

136
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
IT WILL BE OF NO USE TO US
IF 20 SUCH SHOULD COME

137
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
SINCE YOU WILL NOT VISIT THEM.

138
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
DEPEND UPON IT, MY DEAR--

139
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:33,000
WHEN THERE ARE 20,
I'LL VISIT THEM ALL.

140
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:39,000
YOU SEE, JANE!
HE WILL NOT BE PREVAILED UPON.

141
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:43,000
OH, IF ONLY WE'D BEEN ABLE
TO HAVE SONS!

142
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
MISFORTUNES,
WE ARE TOLD

143
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,000
ARE SENT TO TEST OUR FORTITUDE.

144
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:53,000
AND THEY OFTEN REVEAL THEMSELVES
AS BLESSINGS IN DISGUISE.

145
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:58,000
LORD, I'M SO HUNGRY!

146
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:03,000
( bird calling outside )

147
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
IF I COULD LOVE A MAN

148
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:12,000
WHO WOULD LOVE ME ENOUGH TO
TAKE ME FOR A MERE £50 A YEAR

149
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,000
I SHOULD BE VERY WELL PLEASED.

150
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
YES.

151
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
BUT SUCH A MAN
COULD HARDLY BE SENSIBLE

152
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
AND I COULD NEVER LOVE A MAN
OUT OF HIS WITS.

153
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:26,000
OH, LIZZY.

154
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
A MARRIAGE
WHERE EITHER PARTNER

155
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:33,000
CANNOT LOVE
OR RESPECT THE OTHER...

156
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
THAT CANNOT BE AGREEABLE...

157
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
TO EITHER PARTY.

158
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
AS WE HAVE DAILY PROOF.

159
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,000
BUT BEGGARS, YOU KNOW,
CANNOT BE CHOOSERS!

160
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
WE ARE NOT VERY
POOR, LIZZY.

161
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:50,000
WITH FATHER'S ESTATE ENTAILED
AWAY FROM THE FEMALE LINE

162
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
WE HAVE LITTLE
BUT OUR CHARMS

163
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,000
TO RECOMMEND US.

164
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
ONE OF US, AT LEAST

165
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,000
WILL HAVE TO MARRY
VERY WELL.

166
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:00,000
AND SINCE YOU ARE FIVE TIMES
AS PRETTY AS THE REST OF US

167
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
AND HAVE
THE SWEETEST DISPOSITION

168
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
THE TASK WILL FALL ON YOU
TO RAISE OUR FORTUNES.

169
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,000
BUT, LIZZY...

170
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
I WOULD WISH...

171
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
I SHOULD SO MUCH LIKE...

172
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
TO MARRY FOR LOVE.

173
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
AND SO YOU SHALL!

174
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
I AM SURE.

175
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
ONLY, TAKE CARE
YOU FALL IN LOVE

176
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
WITH A MAN
OF GOOD FORTUNE.

177
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
WELL, I SHALL TRY--

178
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
TO PLEASE YOU.

179
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,000
AND YOU?

180
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
I AM DETERMINED

181
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
THAT NOTHING BUT
THE VERY DEEPEST LOVE

182
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
WILL INDUCE ME
INTO MATRIMONY.

183
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
SO...

184
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
I SHALL END AN OLD MAID

185
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:44,000
AND TEACH YOUR TEN CHILDREN
TO EMBROIDER CUSHIONS

186
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:49,000
AND PLAY THEIR
INSTRUMENTS VERY ILL!

187
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
GOOD NIGHT, MAMMA.

188
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:04,000
MY HEAD IS
VERY ILL TONIGHT.

189
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
I WOULDN'T DANCE WITH HIM.

190
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
GOOD NIGHT, LYDIA.
GOOD NIGHT, KITTY.

191
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:13,000
GOOD NIGHT, LIZZY.

192
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
LIZZY!

193
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:05,000
WAIT TILL YOU HEAR OUR NEWS!

194
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
MR. BINGLEY IS
COME TO NETHERFIELD.

195
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
SIR WILLIAM LUCAS
CALLED ON HIM!

196
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
SAVE YOUR BREATH--
I WILL TELL MAMMA.

197
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
I DO NOT WISH TO KNOW.

198
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
WHAT SHOULD WE CARE
FOR MR. BINGLEY

199
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
SINCE WE ARE NEVER
TO BE ACQUAINTED WITH HIM?

200
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
BUT MAMMA!

201
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
DON'T KEEP COUGHING SO,
KITTY.

202
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,000
FOR HEAVEN'S SAKE, HAVE
COMPASSION ON MY NERVES!

203
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
HE HAS 4O SERVANTS!
I DON'T COUGH FOR
MY OWN AMUSEMENT!

204
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,000
HE'S HANDSOME.

205
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,000
HE DECLARED

206
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
HE LOVES
TO DANCE.

207
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Lydia:
HE'S COMING
TO THE NEXT BALL!

208
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
AND BRING SIX LADIES
AND FOUR GENTLEMEN!

209
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
12 LADIES
AND SEVEN GENTLEMEN!

210
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
TOO MANY LADIES.

211
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
Mamma:
I BEG
YOU WOULD STOP

212
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
FOR WE ARE NEVER
TO KNOW MR. BINGLEY

213
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
AND IT PAINS ME
TO HEAR OF HIM.

214
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
I AM SICK OF MR. BINGLEY!

215
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
I AM SORRY
TO HEAR THAT.

216
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
IF I'D KNOWN AS MUCH
THIS MORNING

217
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
I SHOULD NEVER
HAVE CALLED ON HIM.

218
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,000
YOU HAVE
CALLED ON HIM?!

219
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
WE CANNOT ESCAPE
THE ACQUAINTANCE NOW.

220
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:05,000
OH, MY DEAR MR. BENNET!

221
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
HOW GOOD
YOU ARE TO US!

222
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,000
WELL, WELL.

223
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,000
GIRLS! GIRLS!

224
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
IS HE NOT
A GOOD FATHER?

225
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,000
AND NEVER TO TELL US!

226
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,000
WHAT A GOOD JOKE!

227
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,000
AND NOW YOU SHALL ALL
DANCE WITH MR. BINGLEY.

228
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Lizzy:
I HOPE HE HAS

229
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
A STRONG
CONSTITUTION, MAMMA.

230
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,000
AND A FONDNESS FOR
SILLY, YOUNG WOMEN.

231
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
OH, MY DEAR
MR. BENNET.

232
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
NOTHING YOU SAY SHALL
EVER VEX ME AGAIN.

233
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
I'M SORRY TO HEAR IT.

234
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
WELL, KITTY.

235
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:38,000
I THINK YOU MAY COUGH
AS MUCH AS YOU CHOOSE NOW.

236
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:02,000
( lively dance music
playing inside )

237
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
SHALL WE BE
QUITE SAFE HERE

238
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
MR. DARCY,
DO YOU THINK?

239
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:22,000
DAMNED SILLY WAY
TO SPEND AN EVENING.

240
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:11,000
( music ends; applause )

241
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:18,000
( hall falls silent )

242
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:26,000
MR. BINGLEY.

243
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
ALLOW ME THE PLEASURE
OF WELCOMING YOU

244
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
TO OUR LITTLE ASSEMBLY HERE.

245
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
SIR WILLIAM.

246
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
I'M VERY GLAD TO SEE YOU.

247
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
THERE'S NOTHING
THAT I LOVE BETTER

248
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
THAN A COUNTRY DANCE.

249
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:42,000
( music begins again )

250
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
ONLY TWO LADIES,
AFTER ALL.

251
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,000
WHO ARE THEY,
CHARLOTTE?

252
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
MR. BINGLEY'S
SISTERS

253
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
I UNDERSTAND.

254
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
ONE IS MARRIED
TO A MR. HURST.

255
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
THE TALLER GENTLEMAN?

256
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Charlotte:
NO, THE OTHER.

257
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Lizzy:
BETTER
AND BETTER.

258
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
THEY'RE VERY ELEGANT.

259
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
BETTER PLEASED

260
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,000
WITH THEMSELVES THAN
WITH WHAT THEY SEE.

261
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Mrs. Bennet:
LIZZY! JANE!

262
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:09,000
COME HERE!

263
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
YOU SEE
THAT GENTLEMAN THERE?

264
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:15,000
LADY LUCAS HAS JUST TOLD ME
HE IS MR. BINGLEY'S

265
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,000
OLDEST FRIEND.

266
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,000
HIS NAME IS DARCY,
AND HE HAS

267
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
A MIGHTY FORTUNE

268
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
AND A GREAT ESTATE
IN DERBYSHIRE.

269
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
BINGLEY'S WEALTH
IS NOTHING TO HIS!

270
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
10,000 A YEAR

271
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
AT LEAST!

272
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
DON'T YOU THINK
HE'S THE HANDSOMEST MAN

273
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
YOU HAVE EVER SEEN,
GIRLS?

274
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
I WONDER IF HE'D
BE SO HANDSOME

275
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
IF HE WAS NOT
QUITE SO RICH.

276
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Mrs. Bennet:
LIZZY, OH, LORD...

277
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:43,000
THEY'RE COMING OVER.
SMILE, GIRLS!

278
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
MRS. BENNET, MR. BINGLEY
HAS EXPRESSED A WISH

279
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
TO BECOME ACQUAINTED WITH YOU
AND YOUR DAUGHTERS.

280
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:54,000
SIR, THAT IS VERY
GOOD OF YOU.

281
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,000
THIS IS JANE, MY ELDEST,
AND ELIZABETH.

282
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
AND MARY SITS OVER THERE

283
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
AND KITTY
AND LYDIA, MY YOUNGEST

284
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:09,000
YOU SEE THERE DANCING.

285
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
DO YOU LIKE
TO DANCE YOURSELF?

286
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,000
THERE IS NOTHING
I LOVE BETTER, MADAM.

287
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,000
AND IF MISS BENNET
IS NOT OTHERWISE ENGAGED

288
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
MAY I BE SO BOLD
AS TO CLAIM

289
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
THE NEXT
TWO DANCES?

290
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
I AM NOT ENGAGED, SIR.

291
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
GOOD.

292
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
YOU DO US
GREAT HONOR, SIR.

293
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,000
THANK THE GENTLEMAN,
JANE.

294
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,000
MAMMA.

295
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
AND YOU, SIR--

296
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
ARE YOU FOND
OF DANCING, TOO?

297
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
OH, I BEG YOUR PARDON.

298
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
MRS. BENNET, MAY I PRESENT
MY FRIEND, MR. DARCY?

299
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
YOU ARE VERY WELCOME
TO HERTFORDSHIRE.

300
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
AND I HOPE YOU HAVE COME HERE
EAGER TO DANCE

301
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
AS YOUR FRIEND HAS?

302
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:53,000
THANK YOU, MADAM,
I RARELY DANCE.

303
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
WELL, LET THIS BE ONE
OF THE OCCASIONS, SIR

304
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:58,000
FOR I WAGER YOU'LL NOT EASILY
FIND SUCH LIVELY MUSIC

305
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:03,000
OR SUCH PRETTY PARTNERS.

306
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:12,000
UM, PRAY,
EXCUSE ME, MA'AM.

307
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,000
WELL!

308
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:17,000
DID YOU EVER MEET SUCH
A PROUD, DISAGREEABLE MAN?

309
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
MAMMA, HE WILL HEAR YOU.

310
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
I DON'T CARE
IF HE DOES!

311
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
AND HIS FRIEND DISPOSED
TO BE SO AGREEABLE

312
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
AND EVERYTHING CHARMING.

313
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
WHO IS HE TO THINK HIMSELF
SO FAR ABOVE HIS COMPANY?

314
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
THE RICH CAN AFFORD

315
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
TO GIVE OFFENSE
WHEREVER THEY GO.

316
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
WE NEED NOT CARE
FOR HIS GOOD OPINION.

317
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,000
NO, INDEED!

318
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:40,000
PERHAPS HE IS NOT
SO VERY HANDSOME, AFTER ALL.

319
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
NO, INDEED,
QUITE ILL-FAVORED.

320
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:48,000
CERTAINLY NOTHING AT ALL
TO MR. BINGLEY.

321
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:58,000
( music playing )

322
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:48,000
( music continues )

323
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,000
I WONDER AT KITTY AND LYDIA.

324
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,000
THEY'RE SO FOND OF DANCING.

325
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
I TAKE LITTLE PLEASURE
IN A BALL.

326
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Lizzy:
I'D TAKE MORE PLEASURE
IN THIS ONE

327
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
IF THERE WERE
ENOUGH PARTNERS
AS AGREEABLE AS JANE'S.

328
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,000
I BELIEVE THE REWARDS
OF OBSERVATION

329
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:40,000
AND REFLECTION
ARE MUCH GREATER.

330
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
AND SO THEY ARE
WHEN THERE ARE NONE
OTHERS TO BE HAD.

331
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:47,000
WE SHALL HAVE TO BE
PHILOSOPHERS, MARY.

332
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:52,000
( applause )

333
00:18:56,000 --> 00:19:00,000
( music begins )

334
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:05,000
COME, DARCY,
I MUST HAVE YOU DANCE.

335
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
I MUST,
I HATE TO SEE YOU

336
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
STANDING ABOUT
IN THIS STUPID MANNER.

337
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
COME, YOU'D
MUCH BETTER DANCE.

338
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
I CERTAINLY SHALL NOT.

339
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
AT AN ASSEMBLY SUCH AS THIS?

340
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:19,000
IT WOULD BE INSUPPORTABLE.

341
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:23,000
YOUR SISTERS
ARE ENGAGED AT PRESENT

342
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
AND IT WOULD BE
A PUNISHMENT TO ME

343
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
TO STAND UP WITH
ANY OTHER WOMAN IN THE ROOM.

344
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:31,000
DARCY, I WOULDN'T BE AS
FASTIDIOUS AS YOU ARE

345
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,000
FOR A KINGDOM!

346
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
UPON MY HONOR

347
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,000
I NEVER MET SO MANY
PLEASANT GIRLS IN MY LIFE.

348
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,000
AND SEVERAL OF THEM
UNCOMMONLY PRETTY, EH?

349
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
YOU HAVE BEEN DANCING WITH

350
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
THE ONLY HANDSOME GIRL
IN THE ROOM.

351
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:47,000
DARCY, SHE IS THE MOST
BEAUTIFUL CREATURE

352
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
I EVER BEHELD.

353
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
LOOK, LOOK...

354
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
THERE'S ONE
OF HER SISTERS.

355
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,000
SHE'S VERY PRETTY, TOO

356
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:59,000
AND I DARESAY,
VERY AGREEABLE.

357
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Darcy:
SHE IS TOLERABLE,
I SUPPOSE

358
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
BUT SHE'S NOT HANDSOME
ENOUGH TO TEMPT ME.

359
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,000
BINGLEY, I'M IN NO HUMOR
TO GIVE CONSEQUENCE

360
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,000
TO YOUNG LADIES WHO
ARE SLIGHTED BY OTHER MEN.

361
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
GO BACK TO YOUR PARTNER,
ENJOY HER SMILES.

362
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:17,000
YOU'RE WASTING YOUR TIME
WITH ME.

363
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:33,000
( woman laughing )

364
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:39,000
( conversation not audible )

365
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:48,000
( music continues )

366
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Mrs. Bennet:
AND JANE WAS SO ADMIRED!

367
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:33,000
THERE WAS NOTHING LIKE IT.

368
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,000
LORD, I'M FAGGED.

369
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,000
WE DANCED EVERY DANCE.

370
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
AND MARY NONE.

371
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
YES, AND MR. BINGLEY
FAVORED JANE

372
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
ABOVE EVERY OTHER GIRL

373
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,000
FOR HE DANCED
THE FIRST TWO WITH HER

374
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,000
AND THEN THE NEXT
WITH CHARLOTTE LUCAS

375
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
WHICH VEXED ME GREATLY, BUT LO

376
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:51,000
THERE IN THE VERY NEXT

377
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
NOTHING WOULD PLEASE HIM
BUT TO STAND UP WITH JANE AGAIN.

378
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,000
THEN HE DANCED WITH LIZZY

379
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,000
AND WHAT DO YOU THINK
HE DID NEXT?

380
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
ENOUGH, MADAM!

381
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
LET'S HEAR NO MORE
OF HIS PARTNERS.

382
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:04,000
WOULD HE HAD SPRAINED HIS ANKLE
IN THE FIRST DANCE.

383
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:07,000
OH, AND HIS SISTERS--

384
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,000
OH, SUCH
CHARMING WOMEN.

385
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,000
SO ELEGANT AND OBLIGING.

386
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,000
OH, I WISH YOU HAD SEEN THEM.

387
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:13,000
I DARESAY THE LACE

388
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:15,000
ON MRS. HURST'S
GOWN ALONE...

389
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:18,000
NO LACE, NO LACE,
MRS. BENNET, I BEG YOU.

390
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,000
BUT THE MAN HE BROUGHT WITH HIM

391
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
MR. DARCY,
AS HE CALLS HIMSELF

392
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,000
IS NOT WORTH OUR CONCERN

393
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:27,000
THOUGH HE MAY BE THE
RICHEST MAN IN DERBYSHIRE.

394
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,000
THE PROUDEST, THE MOST
HORRID, DISOBLIGING...

395
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:33,000
HE SLIGHTED POOR LIZZY,
YOU KNOW

396
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:36,000
AND FLATLY REFUSED
TO STAND UP WITH HER.

397
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
SLIGHTED MY LIZZY, DID HE?

398
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,000
I DIDN'T CARE
FOR HIM EITHER, FATHER

399
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,000
SO IT'S OF LITTLE MATTER.

400
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,000
Mrs. Bennet:
I WOULD NOT DANCE

401
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:46,000
WITH HIM IF HE SHOULD ASK YOU.

402
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:51,000
I MAY SAFELY PROMISE YOU
NEVER TO DANCE WITH MR. DARCY.

403
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:56,000
AND SO, NONE OF THE
HERTFORDSHIRE LADIES

404
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
COULD PLEASE YOU,
MR. DARCY?

405
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:01,000
NOT EVEN THE FAMOUS
MISS BENNETS?

406
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
WELL,
I NEVER MET

407
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,000
WITH
PLEASANTER
PEOPLE

408
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,000
OR PRETTIER GIRLS
IN MY LIFE.

409
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,000
BINGLEY, YOU ASTONISH ME.

410
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
I SAW LITTLE BEAUTY

411
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,000
AND NO BREEDING AT ALL.

412
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:13,000
THE, ER, ELDEST MISS BENNET IS,
I GRANT YOU, VERY PRETTY.

413
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,000
A FINE CONCESSION.

414
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,000
ADMIT IT, SHE'S AN ANGEL.

415
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,000
SHE SMILES TOO MUCH.

416
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,000
OH, JANE BENNET
IS A SWEET GIRL.

417
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
BUT THE MOTHER!

418
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
( clock chiming )

419
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
I HEARD
ELIZA BENNET DESCRIBED

420
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
AS A FAMOUS
LOCAL BEAUTY.

421
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
WHAT DO YOU SAY
TO THAT, MR. DARCY?

422
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:32,000
I SHOULD AS SOON
CALL HER MOTHER A WIT.

423
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
OH, MR. DARCY,
THAT'S TOO CRUEL.

424
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:38,000
DARCY, I SHALL NEVER UNDERSTAND
WHY YOU GO THROUGH THE WORLD

425
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:39,000
DETERMINED TO BE DISPLEASED

426
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:42,000
WITH EVERYTHING
AND EVERYONE IN IT.

427
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,000
AND I WILL
NEVER UNDERSTAND

428
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,000
WHY YOU ARE
IN SUCH A RAGE

429
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:48,000
TO APPROVE OF EVERYTHING
AND EVERYONE THAT YOU MEET.

430
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:51,000
YOU SHALL NOT MAKE ME THINK ILL
OF MISS BENNET, DARCY.

431
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:53,000
INDEED, HE SHALL NOT.

432
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:56,000
I SHALL DARE
HIS DISAPPROVAL

433
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,000
AND DECLARE HER
A DEAR, SWEET GIRL

434
00:23:58,000 --> 00:23:59,000
DESPITE HER RELATIONS

435
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:01,000
AND I SHOULD NOT BE SORRY
TO KNOW HER BETTER.

436
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,000
NO, NOR I.

437
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:06,000
YOU SEE, MR. DARCY,
WE ARE NOT AFRAID OF YOU.

438
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:08,000
I WOULD NOT HAVE YOU SO.

439
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,000
( snorting )

440
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,000
WHAT...?

441
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,000
AYE, VERY TRUE.

442
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:17,000
A DAMN TEDIOUS WASTE
OF AN EVENING.

443
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:20,000
HE'S JUST WHAT A YOUNG MAN
OUGHT TO BE, LIZZY.

444
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,000
SENSIBLE, LIVELY...

445
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:25,000
...AND I NEVER SAW
SUCH HAPPY MANNERS.

446
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,000
HANDSOME, TOO--

447
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,000
WHICH A YOUNG MAN
OUGHT TO BE IF HE CAN.

448
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:29,000
AND HE SEEMS
TO LIKE YOU VERY MUCH

449
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,000
WHICH SHOWS GOOD JUDGMENT.

450
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,000
I GIVE YOU LEAVE
TO LIKE HIM.

451
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,000
YOU'VE LIKED
MANY A STUPIDER PERSON.

452
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,000
DEAR LIZZY.

453
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:37,000
HE COULD BE HAPPIER

454
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:39,000
IN HIS CHOICE
OF SISTERS AND FRIENDS

455
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,000
THOUGH THE SISTERS
HE CANNOT HELP.

456
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:42,000
DID YOU NOT LIKE THEM?

457
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:45,000
NO, THEIR MANNERS
ARE QUITE DIFFERENT FROM HIS.

458
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:47,000
AT FIRST, PERHAPS,
BUT AFTER A WHILE

459
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,000
I FOUND THEM VERY PLEASING.

460
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
MISS BINGLEY IS TO KEEP
HOUSE FOR HER BROTHER.

461
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:53,000
I'M SURE THEY WILL BE
VERY CHARMING NEIGHBORS.

462
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:55,000
ONE OF THEM MAY BE.

463
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:57,000
NO, LIZZY,
I'M SURE YOU'RE WRONG.

464
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:59,000
AND EVEN MR. DARCY,
YOU KNOW

465
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,000
MAY IMPROVE ON
CLOSER ACQUAINTANCE.

466
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,000
DO YOU MEAN
HE'LL BE IN HUMOR

467
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,000
TO GIVE CONSEQUENCE
TO YOUNG LADIES

468
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:07,000
WHO ARE SLIGHTED
BY OTHER MEN? NEVER!

469
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:10,000
( imitating Darcy ):
"SHE IS TOLERABLE,
I SUPPOSE

470
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:14,000
BUT NOT HANDSOME ENOUGH
TO TEMPT ME."

471
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,000
IT WAS VERY WRONG
OF HIM TO SPEAK SO.

472
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:21,000
INDEED IT WAS--
A CAPITAL OFFENSE.

473
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:25,000
OH, LOOK, CHARLOTTE IS COME.

474
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,000
CHARLOTTE!

475
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:27,000
LIZZY!

476
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:29,000
MY FATHER IS TO GIVE A PARTY
AT LUCAS LODGE

477
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:34,000
AND YOU ARE ALL INVITED.

478
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:38,000
Mr. Lucas:
I HOPE THIS WILL BE THE FIRST
OF MANY OCCASIONS

479
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:41,000
WHEN LUCAS LODGE
WILL BE GRACED
WITH YOUR PRESENCE.

480
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:43,000
HERE, YOU SEE,
WE'RE ALL EASY

481
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:45,000
WITH NO AWKWARDNESS
OR CEREMONY.

482
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,000
QUITE.

483
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:51,000
OH, YES, MY DEAR.
5,000 A YEAR.

484
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:58,000
A MOST AGREEABLE YOUNG MAN!

485
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:10,000
AND HE WOULD DANCE EVERY DANCE
WITH JANE.

486
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:11,000
NOTHING ELSE WOULD DO.

487
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:14,000
AND ARE YOU PLEASED
WITH HERTFORDSHIRE,
COLONEL FORSTER?

488
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,000
VERY MUCH SO, LADY LUCAS.

489
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:17,000
AND NEVER MORE SO
THAN THIS EVENING.

490
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:18,000
A REGIMENT OF INFANTRY
DOESN'T FIND

491
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,000
A READY WELCOME
EVERYWHERE.

492
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:24,000
I THINK YOUR OFFICERS
WILL BE VERY WELL PLEASED.

493
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:26,000
( laughter in distance )

494
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:30,000
THEY SEEM VERY
WELL PLEASED ALREADY.

495
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:32,000
NO DOUBT
YOU ATTEND ASSEMBLIES

496
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:34,000
AT ST. JAMES'S COURT,
MISS BINGLEY?

497
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:36,000
WE GO BUT RARELY, SIR.

498
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:37,000
INDEED,
I AM SURPRISED.

499
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:39,000
I SHOULD BE HAPPY

500
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:41,000
TO INTRODUCE YOU THERE,
YOU KNOW

501
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:43,000
AT ANY TIME
WHEN I'M IN TOWN.

502
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:48,000
YOU'RE TOO KIND, SIR.

503
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,000
WELL... WELL.

504
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:51,000
GOOD... AH, GOOD.

505
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:54,000
CAPITAL, CAPITAL.

506
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:56,000
Miss Bingley:
THE INSUFFERABLE CONCEIT.

507
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:59,000
TO IMAGINE THAT WE'D NEED
HIS ASSISTANCE IN SOCIETY.

508
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:02,000
I AM SURE HE
IS A VERY GOOD
SORT OF MAN, CAROLINE.

509
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:05,000
AND I AM SURE HE KEPT
A VERY GOOD SORT OF SHOP

510
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:07,000
BEFORE HIS ELEVATION
TO THE KNIGHTHOOD.

511
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:09,000
( laughing )

512
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:14,000
POOR DARCY, WHAT AGONIES
HE MUST BE SUFFERING.

513
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:21,000
( stately music playing )

514
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:27,000
( laughing )

515
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,000
ARE YOU IN MERYTON
TO SUBDUE

516
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,000
THE DISCONTENTED
POPULACE, SIR?

517
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:37,000
OR DO YOU DEFEND
HERTFORDSHIRE

518
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:39,000
AGAINST THE FRENCH?

519
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:40,000
NEITHER, MA'AM, I TRUST.

520
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,000
WE HOPE TO WINTER
PEACEFULLY HERE.

521
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:44,000
MY SOLDIERS ARE IN
NEED OF TRAINING.

522
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:47,000
AND MY OFFICERS IN EVER
GREAT NEED OF SOCIETY.

523
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:49,000
THEN AS SOON
AS YOU ARE SETTLED

524
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,000
I HOPE YOU
WILL GIVE A BALL.

525
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:52,000
OH, YES, MY DEAR, DO.

526
00:27:52,000 --> 00:27:54,000
YOU THINK A BALL
WOULD BE WELL RECEIVED?

527
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,000
A BALL?
WHO'S GIVING A BALL?

528
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:58,000
I LONG FOR A BALL
AND SO DOES DENNY.

529
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:00,000
AND SANDERSON...
DON'T YOU?

530
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:03,000
I D-DO INDEED,
MOST PASSIONATELY.

531
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:05,000
AH, LITTLE SANDERSON,
I KNEW YOU WOULD.

532
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:07,000
MAKE HIM GIVE A BALL,
MRS. FORSTER.

533
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:09,000
WE'LL DANCE WITH
ALL THE OFFICERS.

534
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,000
IF MARY WOULD
PLAY SOMETHING

535
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:12,000
WE COULD DANCE
WITH THEM NOW.

536
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:14,000
MARY, NO MORE
OF THAT DULL STUFF.

537
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:16,000
PLAY SOMETHING JOLLY,
WE WANT TO DANCE!

538
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:19,000
BUT THERE ARE STILL
TWO MOVEMENTS... MAMMA!

539
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,000
TELL THEM IT
ISN'T FAIR.

540
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:23,000
OH, PLAY A JIG, MARY--

541
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:28,000
NO ONE WANTS
YOUR CONCERTOS HERE.

542
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:32,000
I FEAR THEIR TASTE IS NOT AS
FINE AS YOURS AND MINE, MARY.

543
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:33,000
BUT LET US OBLIGE THEM

544
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:37,000
FOR NO ONE HERE
PLAYS AS WELL AS YOU.

545
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:38,000
VERY WELL, THOUGH YOU KNOW

546
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:42,000
IT GIVES ME LITTLE PLEASURE.

547
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:44,000
JANE! MR. BINGLEY!
COME DANCE WITH US.

548
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,000
NOT NOW, LYDIA.

549
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:50,000
CAPITAL, CAPITAL!

550
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:56,000
( begins playing lively tune )

551
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,000
I SEE THAT MR. BINGLEY

552
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:03,000
CONTINUES HIS ATTENTIONS
TO JANE, LIZZY.

553
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:06,000
I'M VERY HAPPY FOR HER,
CHARLOTTE.

554
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,000
SHE DOES SEEM
VERY WELL PLEASED WITH HIM.

555
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:10,000
IF HE CONTINUES SO

556
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:12,000
SHE COULD BE VERY MUCH
IN LOVE WITH HIM.

557
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,000
AND MR. BINGLEY?

558
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:16,000
DO YOU THINK HE IS IN LOVE?

559
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:19,000
I THINK IT IS CLEAR
THAT HE LIKES HER VERY MUCH.

560
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:22,000
THEN SHE SHOULD LEAVE HIM
IN NO DOUBT OF HER HEART.

561
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:25,000
SHE SHOULD SHOW MORE AFFECTION
THAN SHE FEELS, NOT LESS

562
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:27,000
IF SHE IS TO SECURE HIM.

563
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:29,000
SECURE HIM? CHARLOTTE.

564
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:33,000
YES, SHE SHOULD SECURE HIM
AS SOON AS MAY BE.

565
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:35,000
BEFORE SHE IS SURE
OF HIS CHARACTER?

566
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:38,000
BEFORE SHE'S EVEN CERTAIN
OF HER OWN REGARD FOR HIM?

567
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:39,000
BUT OF COURSE.

568
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:40,000
HAPPINESS IN MARRIAGE

569
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:43,000
IS ENTIRELY A MATTER
OF CHANCE, YOU KNOW.

570
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:45,000
THERE WILL ALWAYS BE
VEXATION AND GRIEF

571
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:47,000
AND IT IS BETTER
TO KNOW IN ADVANCE

572
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:48,000
AS LITTLE AS POSSIBLE

573
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:51,000
OF THE DEFECTS
OF YOUR MARRIAGE PARTNER.

574
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:53,000
CHARLOTTE,
YOU KNOW IT IS NOT SOUND.

575
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:55,000
YOU WOULD NEVER ACT
LIKE THAT YOURSELF.

576
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:57,000
WELL, IT SEEMS
THAT JANE WILL NOT

577
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:01,000
SO WE MUST HOPE
THAT MR. BINGLEY WILL.

578
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:04,000
I THINK HE GETS LITTLE
ENCOURAGEMENT FROM HIS SISTERS.

579
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:09,000
OR HIS FRIEND.

580
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:12,000
MR. DARCY LOOKS AT YOU
A GREAT DEAL, LIZZY.

581
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:14,000
I CANNOT THINK WHY.

582
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:17,000
UNLESS HE MEANS TO FRIGHTEN ME
WITH HIS CONTEMPT.

583
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:20,000
I WISH HE WOULD NOT
COME INTO SOCIETY.

584
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:21,000
HE ONLY MAKES
PEOPLE UNEASY.

585
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:24,000
WHAT A CHARMING AMUSEMENT
FOR YOUNG PEOPLE

586
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:26,000
THIS IS, MR. DARCY.

587
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:28,000
NOTHING LIKE DANCING,
YOU KNOW.

588
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:31,000
ONE OF THE REFINEMENTS
OF EVERY POLISHED SOCIETY.

589
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:33,000
AND EVERY
UNPOLISHED SOCIETY.

590
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,000
SIR?

591
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:37,000
EVERY SAVAGE CAN DANCE.

592
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:42,000
OH, YES... YES, QUITE.

593
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:44,000
I THINK I SHOULD
SPEAK TO MY SISTER

594
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:47,000
BEFORE SHE EXPOSES US ALL
TO RIDICULE.

595
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:51,000
CAPITAL, CAPITAL!

596
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:53,000
AH, MISS ELIZA.

597
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:55,000
WHY ARE YOU NOT DANCING?

598
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:57,000
MR. DARCY, ALLOW ME

599
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:59,000
TO PRESENT THIS
YOUNG LADY TO YOU

600
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:01,000
AS A VERY
DESIRABLE PARTNER.

601
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:03,000
YOU CANNOT REFUSE
TO DANCE, I AM SURE

602
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:05,000
WHEN SO MUCH BEAUTY
IS BEFORE YOU.

603
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:08,000
INDEED, SIR, I HAVE NOT
THE LEAST INTENTION OF DANCING.

604
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:11,000
PLEASE DON'T SUPPOSE
THAT I MOVED THIS WAY

605
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:13,000
IN ORDER
TO BEG FOR A PARTNER.

606
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,000
I WOULD BE VERY HAPPY

607
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:16,000
IF YOU WOULD DANCE
WITH ME, MISS BENNET.

608
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:21,000
THANK YOU, BUT EXCUSE ME,
I AM NOT INCLINED TO DANCE.

609
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,000
COME, COME, WHY NOT

610
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:25,000
WHEN YOU SEE MR. DARCY
HAS NO OBJECTION

611
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:28,000
ALTHOUGH HE DISLIKES
THE AMUSEMENT

612
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:29,000
SO MUCH IN GENERAL?

613
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:31,000
MR. DARCY IS
ALL POLITENESS.

614
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,000
HE IS, HE IS, AND
WHY SHOULD HE NOT BE

615
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:35,000
CONSIDERING
THE INDUCEMENT?

616
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:37,000
WHO COULD OBJECT
TO SUCH A PARTNER

617
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:38,000
EH, DARCY?

618
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,000
I BEG YOU EXCUSE ME.

619
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:41,000
WELL, WELL...

620
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:45,000
OH, CAPITAL,
LYDIA, CAPITAL!

621
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:50,000
( laughing )

622
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:55,000
I BELIEVE I CAN GUESS
YOUR THOUGHTS AT THIS MOMENT.

623
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:57,000
I SHOULD IMAGINE NOT.

624
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:01,000
YOU ARE THINKING
HOW INSUPPORTABLE IT WOULD BE

625
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:04,000
TO SPEND MANY EVENINGS
IN SUCH TEDIOUS COMPANY.

626
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:07,000
NO, INDEED, MY MIND WAS
MORE AGREEABLY ENGAGED.

627
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:10,000
I HAVE BEEN MEDITATING
ON THE VERY GREAT PLEASURE

628
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:12,000
WHICH A PAIR OF FINE EYES

629
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:14,000
IN THE FACE OF A PRETTY
WOMAN CAN BESTOW.

630
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:18,000
AND MAY ONE DARE ASK
WHOSE ARE THE EYES

631
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:21,000
THAT INSPIRED
THESE REFLECTIONS?

632
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:26,000
MISS ELIZABETH BENNET'S.

633
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:30,000
MISS ELIZABETH BENNET?

634
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:32,000
( chuckling )

635
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:37,000
I AM ALL ASTONISHMENT.

636
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:41,000
( music ends )

637
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:43,000
FROM NETHERFIELD?
OH, JANE!

638
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:45,000
WELL, WHAT
DOES IT SAY?

639
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:47,000
IT IS FROM
MISS BINGLEY.

640
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,000
OH, OH, WELL...

641
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:50,000
THAT IS A GOOD SIGN, TOO.

642
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:53,000
GIVE IT TO ME.

643
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:55,000
"MY DEAR FRIEND."

644
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:57,000
THERE, NOW...

645
00:32:57,000 --> 00:33:00,000
"DINE WITH LOUISA
AND ME TODAY..."

646
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:04,000
LA DI DA, LA DI DA,
DI DA, LA DI DA.

647
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:06,000
"...AS THE GENTLEMEN ARE
TO DINE WITH THE OFFICERS."

648
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:08,000
OH, THAT'S UNLUCKY.

649
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:11,000
STILL, YOU MUST GO
AND MAKE WHAT YOU CAN OF IT.

650
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:13,000
"YOURS EVER, CAROLINE BINGLEY."

651
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:15,000
VERY ELEGANT HAND.

652
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,000
MAY I HAVE THE CARRIAGE, FATHER?

653
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:19,000
Mrs. Bennet:
THE CARRIAGE?
NO, INDEED.

654
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:22,000
YOU MUST GO ON HORSEBACK,
FOR IT LOOKS LIKE RAIN.

655
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:24,000
THEN YOU WILL
HAVE TO STAY THE NIGHT.

656
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,000
MOTHER!

657
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:28,000
Mrs. Bennet:
WHY DO YOU LOOK
AT ME LIKE THAT?

658
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:30,000
WOULD YOU GO ALL THE WAY
TO NETHERFIELD AND BACK

659
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:32,000
WITHOUT SEEING MR. BINGLEY?

660
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,000
NO, INDEED.

661
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:34,000
YOU WILL GO ON NELLIE.

662
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:39,000
THAT WILL DO
VERY WELL INDEED.

663
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:54,000
THERE, LIZZY,
YOU SEE?

664
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:59,000
IT IS ALL EXACTLY
AS I PLANNED.

665
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:17,000
NOW, LET ME SEE
IF I HAVE GOT
THIS RIGHT, JANE--

666
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:21,000
YOUR MOTHER'S SISTER
IS NAMED MRS. PHILIPS?

667
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,000
YES.

668
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:26,000
AND MR. PHILIPS'
ESTATE IS, UM...?

669
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:29,000
HE LIVES IN MERYTON.

670
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:34,000
HE IS AN ATTORNEY.

671
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:38,000
AND YOUR MOTHER'S BROTHER
LIVES IN LONDON?

672
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:40,000
YES.

673
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:43,000
IN GRACECHURCH STREET.

674
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:47,000
IN WHICH PART OF LONDON
IS GRACECHURCH STREET, JANE?

675
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:50,000
I, UM...

676
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:55,000
FORGIVE ME, I...

677
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:57,000
FOSSET, GET HELP.

678
00:34:57,000 --> 00:35:01,000
MISS BENNET IS UNWELL.

679
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:05,000
WELL, MY DEAR, IF JANE
SHOULD DIE OF THIS FEVER

680
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:07,000
IT WILL BE COMFORT TO KNOW

681
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:10,000
THAT IT WAS ALL
IN PURSUIT OF MR. BINGLEY

682
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:11,000
AND UNDER YOUR ORDERS.

683
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:13,000
OH, NONSENSE!

684
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:16,000
PEOPLE DO NOT DIE
OF LITTLE TRIFLING COLDS.

685
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,000
SHE WILL BE
VERY WELL TAKEN CARE OF.

686
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:21,000
MAMMA, I THINK
I MUST GO TO NETHERFIELD.

687
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:22,000
GO TO NETHERFIELD?

688
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,000
NO, THERE'S
NO CALL FOR THAT.

689
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:26,000
JANE IS VERY WELL WHERE SHE IS

690
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:29,000
AND YOU KNOW THERE IS NOTHING
FOR YOU AT NETHERFIELD.

691
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:32,000
YOU HAD MUCH BETTER GO
TO MERYTON WITH YOUR SISTERS

692
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:33,000
AND MEET THE OFFICERS.

693
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:35,000
THERE ARE MORE
THAN ENOUGH TO GO ROUND.

694
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:39,000
I KNOW THAT JANE
WOULD WISH ME TO BE WITH HER.

695
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:41,000
Mr. Bennet:
I SUPPOSE THAT IS A HINT

696
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:42,000
TO SEND FOR THE CARRIAGE?

697
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:44,000
NO, INDEED, FATHER

698
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:46,000
FOR I HAD MUCH RATHER WALK.

699
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:48,000
IT IS BARELY THREE MILES

700
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:50,000
TO NETHERFIELD,
AND I WILL BE BACK FOR DINNER.

701
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:54,000
WALK THREE MILES
IN ALL THAT DIRT?

702
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:56,000
YOU'LL NOT BE FIT
TO BE SEEN.

703
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:59,000
I SHALL BE FIT TO SEE JANE,
WHICH IS ALL I WANT.

704
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:01,000
I AM QUITE DETERMINED, MOTHER.

705
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Kitty:
I KNOW, LIZZY.

706
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:05,000
LYDIA AND I WILL
SET YOU AS FAR
AS MERYTON.

707
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,000
AYE, LET'S CALL
ON DENNY EARLY

708
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:07,000
BEFORE HE IS DRESSED.

709
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:09,000
WHAT A SHOCK HE WILL GET.

710
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:11,000
Both:
MMM...

711
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:13,000
OUR LIFE HOLDS FEW DISTINCTIONS,
MRS. BENNET

712
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:15,000
BUT I THINK
WE MAY SAFELY BOAST

713
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:20,000
THAT HERE SIT TWO OF THE
SILLIEST GIRLS IN THE COUNTRY.

714
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:26,000
GOOD-BYE, LIZZY

715
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:28,000
LOOK, IT'S THAT
CAPTAIN CARTER.

716
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:33,000
COME ON, MAKE HASTE.

717
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:11,000
MISS BENNET.

718
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:14,000
MR. DARCY.

719
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:19,000
I AM COME TO INQUIRE
AFTER MY SISTER.

720
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:20,000
ON FOOT?

721
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:25,000
AS YOU SEE.

722
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:30,000
WOULD YOU BE SO KIND
AS TO TAKE ME TO HER?

723
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:57,000
WELL, WE MUST
ALLOW HER TO BE

724
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:59,000
AN EXCELLENT WALKER,
I SUPPOSE.

725
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:01,000
BUT HER APPEARANCE
THIS MORNING--

726
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:03,000
SHE REALLY LOOKED
ALMOST WILD.

727
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:07,000
Miss Bingley:
I COULD HARDLY
KEEP MY COUNTENANCE.

728
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:09,000
WHAT DOES SHE MEAN BY
SCAMPERING ABOUT THE COUNTRY

729
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:11,000
BECAUSE HER SISTER
HAS A COLD?

730
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:12,000
HER HAIR, LOUISA.

731
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:13,000
HER PETTICOAT.

732
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:16,000
I HOPE YOU SAW
HER PETTICOAT, BROTHER.

733
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:17,000
SIX INCHES DEEP IN MUD.

734
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:19,000
I AM ABSOLUTELY CERTAIN.

735
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:20,000
IT ESCAPED MY NOTICE.

736
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:22,000
SHE LOOKED REMARKABLY WELL.

737
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:25,000
Miss Bingley:
YOU OBSERVED IT,
I AM SURE MR. DARCY.

738
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:27,000
I DID.

739
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,000
I'M INCLINED TO THINK

740
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:31,000
YOU WOULDN'T WISH YOUR SISTER
TO MAKE SUCH AN EXHIBITION.

741
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:33,000
CERTAINLY NOT.

742
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:35,000
IT SEEMS TO ME TO SHOW

743
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:38,000
AN ABOMINABLE SORT
OF CONCEITED INDEPENDENCE.

744
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:40,000
HMM?

745
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:42,000
IT SHOWS A PLEASING
AFFECTION FOR HER SISTER.

746
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:44,000
Miss Bingley:
I'M AFRAID, MR. DARCY

747
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:45,000
THAT THIS ESCAPADE

748
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:47,000
MAY HAVE AFFECTED
YOUR ADMIRATION

749
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:48,000
FOR HER FINE EYES?

750
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:50,000
NOT AT ALL.

751
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:55,000
THEY WERE BRIGHTENED
BY THE EXERCISE.

752
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,000
BUT JANE BENNET
IS A SWEET GIRL.

753
00:38:58,000 --> 00:39:00,000
IT'S VERY SAD
SHE SHOULD HAVE

754
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:02,000
SUCH AN UNFORTUNATE
FAMILY

755
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:03,000
SUCH LOW CONNECTIONS.

756
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:05,000
Miss Bingley:
THEIR UNCLE,
SHE TOLD US

757
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:09,000
IS IN TRADE
AND LIVES IN CHEAPSIDE.

758
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:12,000
PERHAPS WE SHOULD CALL,
WHEN WE ARE NEXT IN TOWN.

759
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:13,000
( both laughing )

760
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:16,000
THEY WOULD BE
JUST AS AGREEABLE TO ME

761
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:18,000
HAD THEY UNCLES ENOUGH
TO FILL ALL CHEAPSIDE.

762
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:20,000
BUT WITH SUCH CONNECTIONS

763
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:23,000
THEY CAN HAVE VERY LITTLE CHANCE
OF MARRYING WELL, BINGLEY.

764
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:28,000
THAT IS THE MATERIAL POINT.

765
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:30,000
Bingley:
MISS BENNET...

766
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:32,000
HOW DOES
YOUR SISTER DO?

767
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:33,000
IS SHE ANY BETTER?

768
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:36,000
I AM AFRAID THAT SHE
IS QUITE UNWELL, MR. BINGLEY.

769
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:37,000
YOU MUST STAY UNTIL

770
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:39,000
YOUR SISTER
IS RECOVERED.

771
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:42,000
OH, I WOULD NOT WISH
TO INCONVENIENCE YOU.

772
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:43,000
Bingley:
I WOULDN'T HEAR OF IT.

773
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:46,000
I'LL SEND TO LONGBOURN
FOR YOUR CLOTHES DIRECTLY.

774
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:48,000
YOU ARE
VERY KIND, SIR.

775
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:53,000
IS THERE TO BE
ANY SPORT TODAY
OR NOT?

776
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:59,000
( birds clucking )

777
00:40:29,000 --> 00:40:30,000
THERE.

778
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:33,000
SHALL I DISGRACE YOU,
DO YOU THINK?

779
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:36,000
YOU LOOK VERY PRETTY, LIZZY

780
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:38,000
AS YOU ARE WELL AWARE.

781
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:40,000
OH, JANE...

782
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:43,000
I HAD MUCH RATHER
STAY HERE WITH YOU.

783
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:46,000
THE SUPERIOR SISTERS
WISH ME MILES AWAY.

784
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:47,000
ONLY YOUR MR. BINGLEY

785
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:50,000
IS CIVIL AND ATTENTIVE.

786
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:53,000
HE IS NOT MY
MR. BINGLEY, LIZZY.

787
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:56,000
OH, I THINK HE IS.

788
00:40:56,000 --> 00:41:01,000
OR HE VERY SOON WILL BE.

789
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:12,000
I BELIEVE
YOU WILL FIND

790
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:14,000
MR. BINGLEY IS IN
THE DRAWING ROOM, MA'AM.

791
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:19,000
THANK YOU.

792
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:51,000
Miss Bingley:
OH, MR. DARCY, COME
AND ADVISE ME, FOR MR. HURST

793
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:52,000
CARRIES ALL
BEFORE HIM.

794
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:53,000
HA!

795
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:58,000
( others groan )

796
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:03,000
MAY I INQUIRE AFTER
YOUR SISTER, MISS BENNET?

797
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:05,000
I THANK YOU.

798
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:06,000
I BELIEVE SHE IS
A LITTLE BETTER.

799
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:08,000
I AM VERY GLAD
TO HEAR IT.

800
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:09,000
OH, MR. HURST

801
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:11,000
I AM QUITE UNDONE.

802
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:14,000
Hurst:
SHOULD HAVE PLAYED THE DEUCE.

803
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:16,000
Miss Bingley:
HE HAS UNDONE US ALL, MR. DARCY.

804
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:19,000
WILL YOU JOIN US,
MISS BENNET?

805
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:20,000
I THANK YOU, NO.

806
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:22,000
YOU PREFER READING
TO CARDS, DO YOU?

807
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:24,000
SINGULAR.

808
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:26,000
Miss Bingley:
MISS BENNET DESPISES CARDS.

809
00:42:26,000 --> 00:42:29,000
SHE IS A GREAT READER
AND HAS NO PLEASURE

810
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:30,000
IN ANYTHING ELSE.

811
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:33,000
I DESERVE NEITHER
SUCH PRAISE NOR SUCH CENSURE.

812
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:38,000
I AM NOT A GREAT READER AND
TAKE PLEASURE IN MANY THINGS.

813
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:44,000
AND WHAT DO YOU
DO SO SECRETLY, SIR?

814
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:48,000
IT IS NO SECRET.

815
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:49,000
I AM WRITING TO MY SISTER.

816
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:51,000
OH, DEAR GEORGIANA!

817
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:53,000
OH, HOW I LONG TO SEE HER.

818
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:55,000
IS SHE MUCH GROWN
SINCE THE SPRING?

819
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:57,000
IS SHE AS TALL AS ME?

820
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:58,000
( all giggling )

821
00:42:58,000 --> 00:43:02,000
SHE IS NOW ABOUT
MISS ELIZABETH BENNET'S HEIGHT

822
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:03,000
OR A LITTLE TALLER.

823
00:43:03,000 --> 00:43:05,000
AND SO ACCOMPLISHED.

824
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:08,000
HER PERFORMANCE
AT THE PIANOFORTE
IS EXQUISITE.

825
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:10,000
DO YOU PLAY, MISS BENNET?

826
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:12,000
AYE, BUT VERY ILL INDEED.

827
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:14,000
Mr. Bingley:
BUT ALL YOUNG LADIES
ARE ACCOMPLISHED.

828
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:16,000
THEY SING,
THEY DRAW, THEY DANCE

829
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:19,000
SPEAK FRENCH AND GERMAN,
COVER SCREENS

830
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:21,000
AND I KNOW NOT WHAT.

831
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:24,000
THERE ARE NOT HALF A DOZEN
WHO WOULD SATISFY MY NOTION

832
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:26,000
OF AN
ACCOMPLISHED WOMAN.

833
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:28,000
Miss Bingley:
NO WOMAN IS ACCOMPLISHED

834
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:32,000
WHO DOES NOT ALSO POSSESS A
CERTAIN SOMETHING IN HER AIR

835
00:43:32,000 --> 00:43:33,000
IN THE MANNER OF WALKING

836
00:43:33,000 --> 00:43:37,000
IN THE TONE OF HER VOICE,
HER ADDRESS AND EXPRESSIONS.

837
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:41,000
Darcy:
AND TO ALL THIS SHE MUST YET
ADD SOMETHING MORE SUBSTANTIAL

838
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:44,000
IN THE IMPROVEMENT OF HER MIND
BY EXTENSIVE READING.

839
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:46,000
I AM NO LONGER SURPRISED

840
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:49,000
AT YOU KNOWING ONLY
SIX ACCOMPLISHED WOMEN

841
00:43:49,000 --> 00:43:50,000
MR. DARCY.

842
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:52,000
I RATHER WONDER
AT YOUR KNOWING ANY.

843
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:56,000
Miss Bingley:
YOU ARE VERY SEVERE
UPON YOUR SEX, MISS BENNET.

844
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:58,000
Lizzy:
I MUST SPEAK AS I FIND.

845
00:43:58,000 --> 00:44:01,000
Miss Bingley:
PERHAPS YOU HAVE
NOT HAD THE ADVANTAGE

846
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:03,000
OF MOVING IN SOCIETY ENOUGH.

847
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:05,000
THERE ARE MANY VERY
ACCOMPLISHED YOUNG LADIES

848
00:44:05,000 --> 00:44:07,000
AMONGST OUR ACQUAINTANCE.

849
00:44:07,000 --> 00:44:09,000
Hurst:
THIS IS A FINE WAY
TO PLAY CARDS.

850
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:10,000
YOU'RE ALL LIGHT.

851
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:15,000
( all sighing )

852
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:24,000
LOOK, GIRLS,
IS IT NOT A FAIR PROSPECT?

853
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:35,000
AND NOW THE MOTHER.

854
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:38,000
ARE WE TO BE INVADED
BY EVERY BENNET IN THE COUNTRY?

855
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:43,000
IT'S TOO MUCH TO BE BORNE.

856
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:48,000
MRS. BENNET,
YOU ARE VERY WELCOME.

857
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:50,000
I HOPE YOU
DO NOT FIND MISS BENNET

858
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:51,000
WORSE THAN YOU EXPECTED.

859
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:53,000
INDEED I DO, SIR.

860
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:55,000
SHE IS VERY ILL INDEED
AND SUFFERS A VAST DEAL.

861
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:57,000
THOUGH WITH THE GREATEST
PATIENCE IN THE WORLD

862
00:44:57,000 --> 00:45:00,000
FOR SHE HAS THE SWEETEST
TEMPER, MR. BINGLEY.

863
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:03,000
BUT SHE IS A GREAT DEAL
TOO ILL TO BE MOVED.

864
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:07,000
WE MUST TRESPASS A LITTLE
LONGER ON YOUR KINDNESS.

865
00:45:07,000 --> 00:45:08,000
BUT OF COURSE.

866
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:12,000
MISS BENNET WILL RECEIVE
EVERY POSSIBLE
ATTENTION, MA'AM

867
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:13,000
I ASSURE YOU.

868
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:15,000
YOU ARE VERY GOOD.

869
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:17,000
WELL, YOU HAVE
A SWEET ROOM HERE.

870
00:45:17,000 --> 00:45:20,000
I THINK YOU WILL NEVER WANT
TO LEAVE NETHERFIELD

871
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:22,000
NOW YOU
ARE COME HERE.

872
00:45:22,000 --> 00:45:25,000
I BELIEVE I SHOULD BE HAPPY
TO LIVE IN THE COUNTRY FOREVER

873
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:27,000
WOULDN'T YOU, DARCY?

874
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:28,000
YOU WOULD?

875
00:45:28,000 --> 00:45:30,000
YOU DON'T FIND THE SOCIETY
SOMEWHAT CONFINED

876
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:32,000
AND UNVARYING
FOR YOUR TASTE?

877
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:35,000
CONFINED AND UNVARYING?

878
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:36,000
INDEED, IT IS NOT, SIR.

879
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:38,000
THE COUNTRY IS A VAST DEAL
PLEASANTER THAN TOWN

880
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:42,000
WHATEVER YOU
MAY SAY ABOUT IT.

881
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:46,000
MAMMA, YOU MISTAKE
MR. DARCY'S MEANING.

882
00:45:46,000 --> 00:45:49,000
DO I? HE SEEMS TO
THINK THE COUNTRY
NOTHING AT ALL.

883
00:45:49,000 --> 00:45:50,000
MAMMA...

884
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:52,000
CONFINED?
UNVARYING?

885
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:53,000
I WOULD HAVE HIM KNOW

886
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:55,000
WE DINE WITH FOUR
AND 20 FAMILIES.

887
00:45:55,000 --> 00:46:00,000
( Miss Bingley
and Mrs. Hurst snorting )

888
00:46:02,000 --> 00:46:04,000
MAMMA?

889
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:07,000
HAVE YOU SEEN
CHARLOTTE LUCAS
SINCE I CAME AWAY?

890
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:10,000
YES, SHE CALLED YESTERDAY
WITH SIR WILLIAM.

891
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:12,000
WHAT AN AGREEABLE MAN HE IS.

892
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:14,000
THAT IS MY IDEA
OF GOOD BREEDING.

893
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:17,000
AND THOSE PERSONS
WHO FANCY THEMSELVES
VERY IMPORTANT

894
00:46:17,000 --> 00:46:19,000
AND NEVER
OPEN THEIR MOUTHS

895
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:23,000
QUITE MISTAKE THE MATTER.

896
00:46:23,000 --> 00:46:25,000
MR. BINGLEY,
DID YOU NOT PROMISE

897
00:46:25,000 --> 00:46:26,000
TO GIVE A BALL
AT NETHERFIELD?

898
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:28,000
IT WILL BE
A GREAT SCANDAL

899
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:30,000
IF YOU DON'T KEEP YOUR WORD.

900
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:32,000
I AM PERFECTLY READY
TO KEEP MY ENGAGEMENT

901
00:46:32,000 --> 00:46:34,000
AND WHEN YOUR SISTER
IS RECOVERED

902
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:35,000
YOU SHALL NAME THE DAY

903
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:36,000
IF YOU PLEASE.

904
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:39,000
OH! THERE NOW, LYDIA.

905
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:41,000
THAT'S A FAIR
PROMISE FOR YOU.

906
00:46:41,000 --> 00:46:45,000
THAT'S GENEROSITY
FOR YOU.

907
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:50,000
THAT'S WHAT I CALL
GENTLEMANLY BEHAVIOR.

908
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:56,000
( sighing )

909
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:22,000
( dog barks )

910
00:47:56,000 --> 00:48:01,000
( dog barking )

911
00:48:37,000 --> 00:48:39,000
MISS ELIZA BENNET.

912
00:48:39,000 --> 00:48:42,000
LET ME PERSUADE YOU
TO FOLLOW MY EXAMPLE

913
00:48:42,000 --> 00:48:44,000
AND TAKE A TURN
ABOUT THE ROOM.

914
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:49,000
IT'S SO REFRESHING.

915
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:59,000
WILL YOU NOT
JOIN US, MR. DARCY?

916
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:02,000
THAT WOULD DEFEAT THE OBJECT.

917
00:49:02,000 --> 00:49:03,000
WHAT DO YOU MEAN, SIR?

918
00:49:03,000 --> 00:49:05,000
WHAT ON EARTH
CAN HE MEAN?

919
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:08,000
Lizzy:
I THINK WE WOULD DO BETTER
NOT TO INQUIRE.

920
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:11,000
NAY, WE INSIST ON KNOWING
YOUR MEANING, SIR.

921
00:49:11,000 --> 00:49:14,000
WHY, THAT YOUR FIGURES APPEAR
TO BEST ADVANTAGE WHEN WALKING

922
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:16,000
AND THAT I MIGHT
BEST ADMIRE THEM

923
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:17,000
FROM MY PRESENT POSITION.

924
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:18,000
OH, SHOCKING!

925
00:49:18,000 --> 00:49:20,000
ABOMINABLE REPLY!

926
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:23,000
HOW SHALL WE PUNISH HIM,
MISS ELIZA?

927
00:49:23,000 --> 00:49:25,000
NOTHING SO EASY.

928
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:26,000
TEASE HIM.

929
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:28,000
LAUGH AT HIM.

930
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:30,000
LAUGH AT
MR. DARCY?

931
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:33,000
IMPOSSIBLE!

932
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:35,000
HE IS A MAN
WITHOUT FAULT.

933
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:37,000
IS HE INDEED?

934
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:40,000
A MAN WITHOUT FAULT?

935
00:49:40,000 --> 00:49:42,000
THAT IS NOT POSSIBLE FOR ANYONE.

936
00:49:42,000 --> 00:49:45,000
BUT IT HAS BEEN MY STUDY
TO AVOID THOSE WEAKNESSES

937
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:48,000
WHICH EXPOSE A STRONG
UNDERSTANDING TO RIDICULE.

938
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:53,000
SUCH AS... VANITY, PERHAPS,
AND PRIDE?

939
00:49:56,000 --> 00:49:58,000
YES, VANITY IS
A WEAKNESS INDEED.

940
00:49:58,000 --> 00:50:01,000
BUT PRIDE--

941
00:50:01,000 --> 00:50:04,000
WHERE THERE IS
A REAL SUPERIORITY OF MIND

942
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:06,000
PRIDE WILL ALWAYS BE

943
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:07,000
UNDER GOOD
REGULATION.

944
00:50:07,000 --> 00:50:09,000
I HAVE FAULTS ENOUGH,
MISS BENNET

945
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:12,000
BUT I HOPE THEY ARE NOT
OF UNDERSTANDING.

946
00:50:12,000 --> 00:50:17,000
MY TEMPER
I CANNOT VOUCH FOR.

947
00:50:19,000 --> 00:50:22,000
IT MIGHT BE CALLED RESENTFUL.

948
00:50:22,000 --> 00:50:25,000
MY GOOD OPINION, ONCE LOST,
IS LOST FOREVER.

949
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:28,000
THAT IS A FAILING, INDEED--

950
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:30,000
BUT I CANNOT LAUGH AT IT.

951
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:33,000
I BELIEVE EVERY DISPOSITION
HAS A TENDENCY

952
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:35,000
TO SOME PARTICULAR EVIL.

953
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:38,000
YOUR DEFECT IS A PROPENSITY
TO HATE EVERYONE.

954
00:50:38,000 --> 00:50:41,000
WHILE YOURS IS WILLFULLY
TO MISUNDERSTAND THEM.

955
00:50:41,000 --> 00:50:46,000
SHALL WE HAVE SOME MUSIC, HMM?

956
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:53,000
( begins playing )

957
00:50:53,000 --> 00:50:58,000
( music playing )

958
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:03,000
GIVE YOUR PARENTS
MY WARMEST SALUTATIONS.

959
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:05,000
AND TELL YOUR FATHER
HE IS MOST WELCOME

960
00:51:05,000 --> 00:51:06,000
TO COME AND SHOOT WITH US

961
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:07,000
AT ANY TIME CONVENIENT.

962
00:51:07,000 --> 00:51:10,000
THANK YOU, SIR,
YOU ARE VERY KIND.

963
00:51:10,000 --> 00:51:13,000
GOOD-BYE.

964
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:18,000
GOOD-BYE.

965
00:51:19,000 --> 00:51:24,000
DRIVE ON, ROSSITER.

966
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:32,000
Miss Bingley:
OH, HOW PLEASANT IT IS

967
00:51:32,000 --> 00:51:37,000
TO HAVE
ONE'S HOUSE TO ONESELF AGAIN.

968
00:51:38,000 --> 00:51:40,000
BUT I FEAR MR. DARCY
IS MOURNING THE LOSS

969
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:42,000
OF MISS ELIZA BENNET'S

970
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:45,000
PERT OPINIONS AND FINE EYES.

971
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:50,000
QUITE THE CONTRARY,
I ASSURE YOU.

972
00:51:56,000 --> 00:51:58,000
Lizzy:
OH, JANE.

973
00:51:58,000 --> 00:52:00,000
I'M SORRY TO SAY IT

974
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:03,000
BUT NOTWITHSTANDING
YOUR EXCELLENT MR. BINGLEY

975
00:52:03,000 --> 00:52:06,000
I'VE NEVER BEEN SO HAPPY
TO LEAVE A PLACE IN MY LIFE.

